WEBVTT

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.490
Misaki Aya-san,

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:37.300
we heard your show in New
York... was a huge success.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:40.860
I expected the critics there to be harsh.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:41.950
I am relieved.

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.450
Congratulations!

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.080
What will you do on your visit home?

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:49.920
Aside from planning my next show,
I will be taking a break.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.460
Do you have any plans?

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:55.590
I am hoping to spend some quality
time with my family.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.830
The triumphant return
of Misaki Aya-san...

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:05.890
currently working primarily abroad...

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:10.680
is the center of both the art and
entertainment world's attention.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.450
Elis, dinner.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.680
Okay.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.610
Misaki Aya-san, the daughter
of Misaki Jiro...

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.630
hero among Japanese painting circles...

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:18.920
and Misaki Shizuka, internationally
famous flutist...

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:22.710
who created a stir among the
world's top orchestras...

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:25.870
is a thoroughbred born in an
artistically talented family.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:25.870
She must be amazing.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.340
She's a graduate of Nadesico Academy.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.160
Have you met her?

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.110
I haven't met her, but her
younger sister is around.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:35.100
She's...

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.100
You mean Misaki-senpai
of the chorus club?

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.210
Was she in the chorus club?

00:02:42.460 --> 00:02:47.260
I haven't spoke to her, but I've seen her
singing behind the school buildings.

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.280
Oh, I've heard about that too.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.950
Misaki-senpai is her sister...

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:58.720
I wonder what it's like growing
up in a house of artists.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.760
There must be a lot of pressure.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:05.230
Pressure?

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:06.990
Hurry up and eat.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:08.430
We'll be late.

00:03:10.550 --> 00:03:12.170
This time already?

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.110
Think about what you want for dinner.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.530
What?

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:19.230
Coming up with a menu's a lot of work.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:24.160
Wait, Onii-chan.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.850
Cobalt Blue Impatience

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.300
I should have brought an umbrella.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:03:59.350
Who is she?

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.830
She'll catch a cold out here.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:35.390
Theme: Chorus Competition Poster

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:35.390
Subject: Free

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:34.640
We'll be choosing some of your paintings
with the chorus club...

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:39.050
to use as posters for their competition.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:41.760
Come up with whatever you want.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.000
What should I do?

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.970
Why does the art club have to make
posters for the chorus club?

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:56.410
Don't be like that.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:04:59.960
Hey.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:00.340
What?

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.710
Look!

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.320
I see.

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.040
Keep going.

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:09.250
Okay!

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:12.140
This contest has already been decided.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:13.870
I'm not going to bother with this.

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.840
Maybe I'll quit, too.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:17.700
Hey, you two...

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:26.280
Very nice. It's interesting.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.860
Thank you.

00:05:28.860 --> 00:05:31.650
I enjoy doing this kind of
thing once in a while.

00:05:31.650 --> 00:05:32.730
Really?

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:35.160
What is Hosen-san drawing?

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:38.450
Well...

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:41.240
It's bold and exciting.

00:05:42.810 --> 00:05:44.190
I see.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.400
See you later.

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:53.760
Good work today.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:57.980
What's wrong with her?

00:05:57.980 --> 00:05:59.200
I know, right?

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:01.140
Good work today.

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:09.270
Hosen-kun! Could I have a word?

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:15.460
You told me to think about
what I wanted to dinner.

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:16.770
I know what I want.

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:18.160
Soba!

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.020
Soba? This isn't about dinner.

00:06:22.430 --> 00:06:25.600
You joined the art club, so why
not get along with everyone?

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:30.030
But the art club members don't
seem to agree with you.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:32.590
I'll do some shopping and head home.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:34.550
Elis.

00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:57.330
Misaki Sumire.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:00.100
What are you doing?

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.260
I was just, uh...

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:05.300
wondering what was going on
inside the auditorium...

00:07:05.510 --> 00:07:06.970
You're Misaki-san, aren't you?

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:10.410
Me? Yes, I am...

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:13.580
You're a member of the
chorus club, right?

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.910
I am. Who are you?

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.400
I'm Elis, a freshman.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.780
Elis-san? Aren't you the special student?

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:26.360
Yes. I'm currently working on
a poster for the chorus club.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.590
The preliminaries are soon, aren't they?

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.010
They are...

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.430
Oh? They're done.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:36.700
Ahem!

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:40.670
No matter how good the
art club's posters are...

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:43.810
the chorus club still has
to give it their best.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:50.380
Excuse me.

00:07:51.560 --> 00:07:52.980
Misaki!

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:56.420
Sorry I'm late.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.060
You're free to go, everyone.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:07:59.030
Okay.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:02.360
Misaki, you know there's no time
left before the competition.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.540
Stay and practice by yourself.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:06.960
Okay.

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:11.660
I don't understand girls of that age.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:15.800
Actually, I don't understand
girls of any age.

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:18.140
You definitely don't.

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:21.250
I don't know what Elis is thinking.

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:24.280
If something's bothering her,
she should just say so.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:27.120
Maybe she doesn't want you to worry.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:30.550
Or else she doesn't think I'm reliable.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.170
She'll be fine.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:36.990
She's much more mature than you think.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:39.630
You think so?

00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:44.370
What I'm worried about is...

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:48.050
You're advising a high school art club...

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:49.810
but you refuse to take up the
brush yourself, Hiroki!

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:53.030
I don't know what you're thinking!

00:08:53.030 --> 00:08:55.730
Well, eventually...

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:57.620
Are you saying you'll start
painting again someday?

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.500
I don't know.

00:09:02.160 --> 00:09:03.290
Maybe.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:10.900
What, do you have a stomachache?

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.430
I'm wondering if I should
write a happy ending.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.870
Let me take a look.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.040
You're basing your writing on Onii-chan.

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:23.980
The love triangle I'm following won't
be resolved any time soon.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.710
What do you think, Elis-chan?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:27.290
I don't know.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.150
I'm impressed you can write this stuff.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:34.590
And I'm impressed you can
paint the stuff you paint.

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:38.620
I'll try drawing a car, but
it just looks like a car.

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:39.760
I don't know what I'm supposed
to be doing.

00:09:40.920 --> 00:09:43.350
This place sure is nice and quiet.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:46.330
I don't need to worry about
what anyone else thinks.

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:50.350
That dog you're drawing is pretty cute.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:53.000
It's a cat.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:58.880
Look what you did.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.850
It's because you suddenly
jumped out of nowhere.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:05.520
You and I both had rough days.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.220
Bye.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:18.060
Huh?

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:22.410
That's nothing to cry about.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.020
Is Earl Grey all right with you?

00:10:38.020 --> 00:10:40.130
Sure.

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:42.950
Thank you for the replacement cakes.

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:49.060
Thank you for walking Sumire home.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:51.260
I hope you don't mind.

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:59.480
Kamikura-san teaches the Nadesico
Academy High School art club.

00:10:59.480 --> 00:11:01.270
I'm not a teacher.

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:03.170
Really? The art club?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:04.790
Father.

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:06.850
I'm just the acting advisor.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.510
I'm currently enrolled in the college.

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:12.020
I'm still in training, helping the high
school art club however I can.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:15.450
Kamikura-san, don't you paint as well?

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:19.660
Paint? Right now, I...

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.530
I'd love to hear the stories of the young.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:27.840
I haven't been in Japan much lately, and
I've fallen behind on worldly affairs.

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:29.830
But Sensei has somewhere to go...

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:35.800
My activites are nothing compared to
everything the Misaki family is doing.

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:37.310
What a charming young man.

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:40.100
Please, make yourself at home.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:45.820
I'd love to stay, but I have soba
waiting for me at home.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:48.910
Kamikura-san, do you like soba?

00:11:48.910 --> 00:11:50.090
Well, I...

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:53.640
Sumire, get some takeout from Senjiran.

00:11:53.640 --> 00:11:54.530
Yes.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:59.200
Give me a break.

00:12:00.090 --> 00:12:01.600
What?

00:12:01.600 --> 00:12:04.030
You ate soba?

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:07.760
I told you we'd be having soba tonight!

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:11.600
What's with the apron?

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.890
What is this?

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:19.620
It's my special soba.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:23.550
I let it simmer for a long time,
so I'm sure it'll taste great.

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:26.480
You boiled it how long?

00:12:29.370 --> 00:12:33.560
You don't want to eat my cooking.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:38.120
You didn't want to eat it, so
you went to Misaki-senpai's.

00:12:38.120 --> 00:12:39.370
That's not it.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:43.340
Damn it, how am I supposed to eat this?

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:45.340
This stuff used to be soba.

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:52.750
Living in that house of elite artists
can't be easy for Sumire.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.020
I wouldn't be able to put up with it.

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:58.700
I don't like Misaki-senpai.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:12:59.350
What?

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:00.310
It's not fair.

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:02.760
She's famous, rich, and
has a fabulous family.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:05.020
What does she have to
be unhappy about?

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.200
Elis...

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:10.720
Hosen-san's was chosen.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.270
No surprise there.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.300
I know, right?

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:17.500
The president's is fine, but I don't
know about Hosen-san's.

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:20.940
I wish I had a kind brother, too.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:23.280
An Onii-sama.

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:24.980
What do you think?

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.350
President?

00:13:26.350 --> 00:13:29.690
I had some doubts, but decided
to submit it as it was.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:32.290
I think it's very interesting.

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:36.000
I didn't know you could paint
something like this.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:37.500
I do every now and then.

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:44.470
Do you think it's right for me
to stay in the art club?

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:45.840
You want to quit?

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.720
That's not what I meant, but...

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.410
Then you should stay.

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:54.840
I like your painting.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:02.890
So do I.

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:06.590
Late again.

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:11.330
We can't have her skipping practice
before the competition.

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:15.000
Could last year's events
still be bothering her?

00:14:15.270 --> 00:14:18.370
In any case, why don't we hear
what Misaki-san has to say.

00:14:18.780 --> 00:14:19.800
Okay.

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:26.310
I've been looking for her, but she didn't
show up to practice today either.

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:31.280
I can't believe she's beaten 25 people.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:37.490
You've got to be joking.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:41.120
Hosen-san? What are you doing?

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.740
I could ask you the same thing.

00:14:43.740 --> 00:14:45.480
Do you have any money?

00:14:45.480 --> 00:14:46.580
What?

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:50.510
I used all my money on games,
and I'm parched.

00:14:51.130 --> 00:14:52.660
I've got some.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:56.120
Delicious.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.310
I'll pay you back tomorrow.

00:14:58.310 --> 00:14:59.100
Sure.

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:01.880
Do you go to arcades often?

00:15:02.390 --> 00:15:05.420
At first I would just watch the boys.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:07.550
Eventually, I figured out how to play.

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.590
I gave it a try and had so much fun.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:13.920
I wonder if your sense of musical rhythm
has anything to do with it.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:19.360
I skipped chorus club practice again.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:22.300
I'll probably have to perform again...

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:24.980
but I don't know what I'll do
if I make another mistake.

00:15:25.490 --> 00:15:26.740
A mistake?

00:15:26.740 --> 00:15:28.980
At last year's chorus competition...

00:15:33.860 --> 00:15:37.180
My family came to watch, and
I was extremely nervous.

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:56.080
My sister and parents told me they didn't
notice, but I knew that couldn't true.

00:15:56.690 --> 00:15:59.400
I'm the outcast of the Misaki family.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:00.780
That's awful.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:04.050
Since then, I haven't been able
to sing in front of people.

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:09.860
Stupid, isn't it? I know I'm pathetic.

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:14.750
I can't use the color red.

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:21.320
When I painted red roses blue,
I was labeled rebellious...

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:23.250
and was ostracized by the art club.

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:26.210
I still can't use red, though.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.150
I saw your poster.

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:32.930
It was wonderful.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:35.330
I may not know what happened to you...

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:38.140
but I hope you'll be able to draw
red roses again someday.

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:46.720
I know you practice singing alone
behind the school buildings.

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:48.830
Oh, no.

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:51.750
Did you hear me singing?

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:54.600
You actually love singing, don't you?

00:16:56.830 --> 00:16:59.260
You always have that turtle with you.

00:16:59.260 --> 00:17:00.620
Yes.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:06.780
It's a charm my sister gave me
after last year's competition.

00:17:06.780 --> 00:17:11.040
She said, “Let's take our time
pursuing our dreams.”

00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:13.220
It's so cute.

00:17:13.220 --> 00:17:17.470
If you can't sing in front of people, why
don't you pretend no one's there?

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:21.520
Not the audience, not your father
or mother, not even your sister.

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:23.420
Pretend they're not there?

00:17:23.420 --> 00:17:26.040
I'm looking forward to the
chorus competition.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:28.290
Hosen-san, without that, I...

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:30.360
You'll be fine.

00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:42.720
National Chorus Competition

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:52.750
What's with the turtle?

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.740
It's a charm.

00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:57.050
The tortoise beat the hare, didn't he?

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:22.500
Misaki.

00:18:22.990 --> 00:18:24.860
Misaki, are you all right?

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:26.020
Yes.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:32.230
Nadesico Academy, get ready.

00:18:32.230 --> 00:18:33.460
Okay.

00:18:35.870 --> 00:18:37.790
Just relax and keep it together.

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:43.290
There they are.

00:18:45.520 --> 00:18:48.040
Huh? That girl has her eyes closed.

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:15.120
Maybe we'll win.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.880
You think so?

00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:18.960
Our singing princess is back.

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.900
They'll hear you inside.

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:26.550
The competition isn't over
yet, so keep quiet.

00:20:32.090 --> 00:20:34.210
Misaki-senpai.

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:35.850
Onee-chan.

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:39.180
Is it too early to congratulate you?

00:20:52.090 --> 00:20:54.830
Did you do something to her?

00:20:55.530 --> 00:20:56.560
It's a secret.

00:20:56.560 --> 00:20:57.270
Hosen-san!

00:21:01.300 --> 00:21:03.140
Thank you, Hosen-san!

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:06.140
I'll pay you back for the juice tomorrow.

00:21:06.600 --> 00:21:08.510
And I'll give it back tomorrow, too.

00:21:08.510 --> 00:21:09.510
Okay.

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:13.570
It's your turn to cook dinner tonight.

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:15.570
I want pasta.

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:16.450
Pasta?

00:21:16.450 --> 00:21:18.140
Yes, pasta.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:19.520
Where did that come from?

00:21:19.730 --> 00:21:22.860
And I won't accept anything
it if it's not al dente.

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:13.870
Moon gray is the solitary color
of the dark side of the moon.

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:16.310
The color of a lonely girl's eyes.

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:17.710
By the way, Onii-chan...

00:23:17.710 --> 00:23:22.420
why do men fall for lonely
girls who put up a front?

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:24.570
Men love surprises.

00:23:24.570 --> 00:23:25.430
I see.

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:26.860
I'm perfect, then!

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:27.800
How are you perfect?

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:29.370
I'm a great painter and
may seem dextrous...

00:23:29.370 --> 00:23:30.540
but I'm a terrible cook.

00:23:30.540 --> 00:23:32.790
That kind of surprise is a huge minus.

00:23:32.790 --> 00:23:34.060
It's not okay?

00:23:34.060 --> 00:23:36.680
Next Episode, “Moon Gray Sigh.”

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:38.780
Love honestly!
